# Native daemon and RPC

The native daemon API in Upwell 0.20 exposes typed RPC services from `upwell::daemon`. A service owns related operations; each `#[rpc]` method receives its request through `Payload<T>`.

<Example title="Define one daemon RPC operation">

```rust plain
use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};
use upwell::daemon::{handlers, rpc, service, Payload};

#[derive(Deserialize)]
struct AddRequest {
    left: i64,
    right: i64,
}

#[derive(Serialize)]
struct AddResponse {
    total: i64,
}
```

Declare the service and its operation:

```rust plain
#[service]
struct Calculator;

#[handlers]
impl Calculator {
    #[rpc]
    async fn add(&self, Payload(request): Payload<AddRequest>) -> AddResponse {
        AddResponse {
            total: request.left + request.right,
        }
    }
}
```

</Example>

Register the service through the daemon application builder used by the binary. This page intentionally limits itself to the released service, handler, and payload form; streaming, generated clients, and other daemon features can differ between historical and 1.0 releases. For an upgraded application, use the [1.0 RPC services guide](/docs/1.0.0/rpc/services).
